//? Title: Vector clocks: actual send/receive state and causal order
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Distributed processes need to distinguish causally related events from
concurrent ones without a shared physical clock. A vector timestamp records the
event counts known from every process.
)

\toc

> The method

A local/send event increments its own component; receive takes componentwise
maximum with the message then increments the receiver component. Under the full
protocol, each component records the latest known count for its process. Thus
a→b implies V(a)≤V(b) with one strict component; conversely the known-count
interpretation reconstructs a causal chain. Distinct incomparable vectors
represent concurrency. Equal vectors are neither strict order nor concurrency.
Cost and message size are O(number of processes).

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vector_clock_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::VectorClock sender(2), receiver(2);
    auto message = a::vc_send(sender, 0);
    a::vc_receive(receiver, 1, message);
    std::print("| actual send | actual receive | happens before |\n|---|---|---|\n|`{}`|`{}`|{}|\n",
               message.v, receiver.v, a::vc_happens_before(message, receiver));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual send {}", message.v));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, "Merge maxima, increment receiver1");
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual receive {}", receiver.v));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/vector_clock_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual send | actual receive | happens before |
|---|---|---|
|`[1, 0]`|`[1, 1]`|true|
\image(figures/vector_clock_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual native producing values from the complete small worked example.)
