> Interpretation and limits

Counters are bounded signed integers, so the increment that would exceed INT_MAX
throws before mutation. Shape mismatches, invalid process IDs and manually
introduced negative counters also throw. Caller synchronization is required.
Comparing arbitrary edited vectors alone cannot establish real-world causality;
that interpretation depends on the event protocol.

The complete editable C++ programs save figures locally; results contain
ordinary computed Markdown. Selected counters describe actual producer
operations, excluding validation when stated.

> References

- Fidge and Mattern vector timestamps; the full event protocol and
  componentwise-order proof are stated above.

